    "canonicalId": 353668451589,
    "operations": 11,
    "equation": "x = y * (((z*x)*((z*x)*z)) * (((z*x)*((z*x)*z))*y))",
    "abbreviation": "u = (z*x)*((z*x)*z); x = y*(u*(u*y))",
    "equivalentAxioms": [
      63,
      1692
    ]
  },
  "proofIdeas": [
    "Let f_y(x)=y*x and g_y(x)=x*(x*y). E63 says f_y g_y=id; E1692 says g_y f_y=id. The new identity joins them as f_y g_y g_z f_z=id with independent y,z.",
    "Six elementary equational substitutions derive E63 from the joined identity. An arbitrary row collision makes g_z f_z have equal values; the joined identity then forces the original inputs equal. Its outer row supplies a preimage of every x. Thus the joined identity is exactly E63 plus left bijectivity, equivalently E63 and E1692.",
    "Actual left division transfers E125 to E63 and vice versa by cancellation. Division of an E125 model has bijective rows and hence satisfies the joined identity. Conversely, the joined identity supplies the division needed to recover an E125 model.",
    "The forward operation is D(x,y)=(x*y)*x and its inverse is x*y=D(y,D(y,x)). These uniform inverse terms give term-structural equivalence and preserve all labelled and unlabelled model counts.",
    "The extra partial-image theorem characterizes actual left divisions of E63 models by E125 on arbitrary carriers. It does not assert that every infinite E63 model has left division."
  ],
  "additionalTheorems": [
    {
      "name": "Parastrophes.Eq125Image.left_term",
